# Give the localizer a coarse pose in the map frame and (re)load the map it
# should register against. Served by localizer_node (SyncAI-Fast-LIO2's
# `localizer`, the one FAST-LIO2 package still in the fork) on the relative
# name `relocalize`, so it lands on <robot_id>/localizer/relocalize. The
# backend calls it for the operator's initial pose and on every map switch.
# Moved here from that repo's `interface` package in 2026-09, the last of its
# services to come over, so that every interface the backend builds against
# is in one package.
#
# SUCCESS IS A RECEIPT, NOT A RESULT. Registration runs asynchronously on the
# localizer's timer with no deadline; this returns once the guess and the map
# are accepted. IsValid (relocalize_check) is the only surface that reports
# whether the registration after this guess actually converged.
#
# The pose is taken RAW, all six degrees of freedom. The `initialpose` topic
# and the INI's [initial_pose] instead go through the localizer's planar-guess
# path, which keeps the current roll / pitch / z and sets only x / y / yaw --
# and that matters, because the lidar mount is tilted and the map is
# gravity-aligned, so a flat 6-DOF guess never passes the rough-registration
# score and the localizer retries forever. A relocalize call is therefore
# normally followed by an `initialpose` publish; the backend's map switch does
# exactly that, in that order.
#
# pcd_path is loaded during the call as a side effect (the localizer also
# loads [map] pcd at construction). Angles are radians.
string pcd_path
float32 x
float32 y
float32 z
float32 yaw
float32 pitch
float32 roll
---
bool success
string message
